Author: thesa <thesa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 7 13:19:44 2026 -0400

    fix(shadow-gates): batch-hoist gate checks, fix shadow-log ordering, close hourly gap
    
    _auto_place_trades() called each of the 5 shadow-only gates (hourly/rain/
    snow/hurricane-count/hurricane-next-event) inline per-ticker instead of
    once per batch, and ran the shadow-routing branches after the placement-
    only checks (validate/caps/Kelly/price/VaR) instead of before them. Hoist
    the gates to once-per-call for a stable batch-wide value, and move shadow
    routing to right after ticker resolution so a shadow-only ticker always
    gets logged for scoring even when it would've failed a later placement-only
    check -- previously that biased the settled-sample floor these gates wait
    on, and wasted a live price refetch + 5000-sim VaR calc on tickers that
    were never going to place.
    
    Also closes a real gap an opus review caught while verifying this: hourly-
    directional temperature markets had no shadow-only enforcement outside the
    cron loop -- paper.check_position_limits() and all 4 of main.py's manual
    placement paths (cmd_order, cmd_paper, _quick_paper_buy, cmd_today's quick-
    place flow) guarded rain/snow/hurricane but never hourly, so a manual
    paper buy on a KXTEMP*H ticker could place regardless of
    _hourly_gates_active(). Added matching guards to all 5.
    
    6 new regression tests: 2 lock in the once-per-batch gate invariant
    (call-count + stateful-flip), 4 cover the new hourly manual-path guards.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

